<</A<</BBox[-115.653 -145.565 840.25 810.337]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>/Alt(Chart on health insurance coverage of the population:\rIn 2018 87.7% \(approximately 72.8 million\) of the total German population of around 83 million were covered by statutory health insurance, 10.5% \(approximately 8.7 million\) had private health insurance and 1.8% \(approximately 1.5 million\) had other forms of health cover. OtherŽ includes people entitled to healthcare provision as recipients of social security benefits, disabled veterans, recipients of support resulting from the equalisation of burdens, free medical or therapeutic care for police and Germanys armed forces, people without health insurance and people who have not stated the existence of health insurance. ␀)/K 826/P 1153 0 R/Pg 653 0 R/S/Figure>>
