<</A 1246 0 R/Alt(Diagram showing how the health fund works.\rThe health fund had a total value of 222,2 billion euros in 2018. Insured individuals pay health insurance contributions amounting to 14.6% of their gross pay, of which 50% each is borne by the employee and the employer. Additional contributions or refunds are possible. The health insurance funds pass the contributions on to the health fund. The government contributes tax-funded subsidies. The Federal Employment Agency and Deutsche Rentenversicherung \(German Pension Insurance\) pay contributions to the fund for unemployed people and pensioners. The fund pays out a basic flat rate per insured individual to the health insurance funds plus extra charges and administrative costs. This is used to pay for medicines or treatments, meaning that the money goes to healthcare providers such as doctors or hospitals.)/K 79/P 1223 0 R/Pg 191 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
